        "w": 12,
        "h": 7
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**This is not the bundled Prometheus.** The chart's Prometheus keeps `retention: 30m` and exists to feed KEDA; it cannot answer a question about yesterday. Point this dashboard at your long-retention store.\n\n**SLI 1 (deployment success rate) is not on this dashboard.** It was built on `ome_inferenceservice_transition_status`, which reports `status.modelStatus.transitionStatus` \u2014 a field written only by the RawDeployment status path. Nothing on the OMENative path sets it, so the ratio silently excluded every OMENative InferenceService while still reporting a confident percentage. Measuring it correctly needs a counter on the readiness edge, which both deployment modes share; until that exists, no number here is better than a wrong one.\n\n**SLI 2 needs the OME control-plane pods scraped** \u2014 `ome_isvc_time_to_ready_seconds` is exported by the controller-manager.\n\nThere is no warm/cold model split here. Model-resident nodes are selected by a hard `nodeSelector`, so a serving pod is only created once the weights are already local \u2014 the download happens before the pod exists and is invisible to this measurement."
